Register the Linux systray integration on all architectures

Thunderbird registers its Rust system tray component only on x86_64
Linux, because the Rust tray depends on the ksni crate only for that
target.

Betterbird's systray patch replaces that component with
nsMessengerUnixIntegration which builds fine on all architectures.

Register nsMessengerUnixIntegration for all Linux targets.

Upstream: https://github.com/Betterbird/thunderbird-patches/pull/623

diff --git a/mailnews/base/src/components.conf b/mailnews/base/src/components.conf
--- a/mailnews/base/src/components.conf
+++ b/mailnews/base/src/components.conf
@@ -320,10 +320,7 @@ elif buildconfig.substs["OS_ARCH"] == "WINNT":
             "headers": ["/comm/mailnews/base/src/nsMessengerWinIntegration.h"],
         },
     ]
-elif (
-    buildconfig.substs["OS_ARCH"] == "Linux"
-    and buildconfig.substs["TARGET_CPU"] == "x86_64"
-):
+elif buildconfig.substs["OS_ARCH"] == "Linux":
     Classes += [
         {
